'''''Persea barbujana''''', the '''Canary laurel''' or '''barbusano''', is a species of tree in the laurel family, [[Lauraceae]]. It is [[Endemism|endemic]] to the [[Macaronesia]]n islands of [[Madeira]] (incl. [[Porto Santo Island|Porto Santo]]) and the [[Canary Islands]].<ref name="iucn status 11 November 2021" /><ref name = powo/> It is often placed as the sole species in genus ''[[Apollonias]]''. Molecular phylogenic analyses found that the species is nested within the genus ''[[Persea]],'' which also includes the Macaronesian endemic ''[[Persea indica]]''.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Li |first1=Lang |last2=Li |first2=Jie |last3=Rohwer |first3=Jens G. |last4=van der Werff |first4=Henk |last5=Wang |first5=Zhi-Hua |last6=Li |first6=Hsi-Wen |date=September 2011 |title=Molecular phylogenetic analysis of the Persea group (Lauraceae) and its biogeographic implications on the evolution of tropical and subtropical Amphi-Pacific disjunctions |url=http://doi.wiley.com/10.3732/ajb.1100006 |journal=American Journal of Botany |language=en |volume=98 |issue=9 |pages=1520–1536 |doi=10.3732/ajb.1100006|pmid=21860056 }}</ref>

The [[La Gomera]] subspecies is distinct and endangered.<ref name="iucn status 11 November 2021" /><ref name=iucn2>{{Cite iucn|title=''Apollonias barbujana'' subsp. ''ceballosi''|author1=Bañares, A.|display-authors=etal|year=1998|article-number=e.T30321A9535286|doi=10.2305/IUCN.UK.1998.RLTS.T30321A9535286.en|access-date=28 July 2024}}</ref>

